## Getting started

```sh
[% if kind == "wasm" -%]
trunk serve            # live-reloading dev server at http://localhost:8080
trunk build --release  # production bundle in ./dist
[%- elif kind == "embedded" -%]
cargo build --release  # cross-compiles for thumbv7em-none-eabihf
# flash/run with your probe, e.g. `cargo run` once you set a runner in .cargo/config.toml
[%- elif kind == "axum" -%]
cargo run              # serves on http://localhost:3000
[%- elif kind == "microservice" -%]
cp .env.example .env   # local config (defaults to a sqlite file)
cargo run              # serves on http://localhost:8080
# create then list an item:
#   curl -sXPOST localhost:8080/items -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"name":"hello"}'
#   curl -s localhost:8080/items
# Architecture, 12-factor mapping, and k8s deploy: see ARCHITECTURE.md
[%- elif kind == "ios" -%]
cargo test             # build & test the Rust core (CI-verified)
bash build-rust.sh     # cross-compile the core into ios/Frameworks/RustCore.xcframework
xcodegen generate      # generate [[ name_pascal ]].xcodeproj from project.yml
open [[ name_pascal ]].xcodeproj   # then ⌘R to run the SwiftUI app in the Simulator
[%- elif kind == "lib" -%]
cargo test             # runs unit tests + doctests
cargo doc --open       # build & view the API docs
[%- else -%]
cargo run -- --help
[%- endif %]
```

## Development

```sh
cargo fmt --all          # format
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings   # lint
cargo test               # test
```
[% if hooks %]
Git pre-commit hooks (in `.githooks/`) run `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy`,
and `cargo check` before every commit. They activate automatically after your
first clone once you run:

```sh
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```
(already configured in this repo by `cargo quickstart`).
